--TEST--
`instanceof` is not a Novis operator: `E0253` refuses it where it is written and names `is` — `rule:php-migration/one-type-test`, `rule:types/type-test`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The one divergence from PHP that no untyped binding makes reachable
// (`rule:php-migration/every-divergence-is-deliberate-and-listed`): it is a
// choice of spelling, taken because one operator answers what PHP splits
// across two. The refused word does not compile, so a converted program pays a
// mechanical rewrite and never a silent change of meaning.
class Animal {}

mixed $pet = new Animal();
echo $pet instanceof Animal, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0253]: `instanceof` is not a Novis operator; the type test is `is`
   --> %s:10:11
   |
10 | echo $pet instanceof Animal, "\n";
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^ no operator is spelled this way
   = help: write `$x is Request`; a class reference on the right is `$x is $cls` (`rule:types/type-test`)

error: aborting due to 1 error
